      "description": "Career-Engaged Learning | Trinity University Skip to main content Utility Menu Apply Visit Give account_circle Info for manage_search Menu Search search Top Searches Main About Trinity Mission and Values Leadership and Governance Our Campus History and Traditions Strategy and Investment Trinity in San Antonio Academics Majors and Minors Pre-Professional Programs Graduate Programs Faculty Schools and Departments Academic Centers Study Abroad Research Faculty Research and Scholarship Undergraduate Research Centers and Facilities Access and Support Student Success Academic Success Accessibility and Accommodations Career-Engaged Learning Inclusion and Belonging Health and Wellbeing Campus Life Housing Dining Sports and Recreation Clubs and Organizations Safety Admissions and Aid Apply to Trinity Visit Campus Cost and Financial Aid Admitted Tigers Connect With Admissions Guides and Resources Utility Menu Apply Visit Give close Resources For Alumni Current Students Athletics Parents Faculty and Staff Prospective Students Visitors How-Tos Update Your Alumni Information Connect with the Trinity Network Volunteer and Give Back Quick Links Alumni Website Submit a Class Note Update My Information Find a Club Near You Request a Transcript Essential Resources Make a Gift Join the LinkedIn Group Share Your Story Buy Trinity Merchandise How-Tos Get Academic Support Find Your Community Solve a Campus Life Problem Quick Links Campus Events Academic Calendar Campus Dining Coates Library Essential Resources MyTU Workday Canvas Student Handbook Student Health Services How-Tos Guide for Student Athletes Quick Links Athletics Website Watch Tiger Network Athletics Instagram Bell Center Hours Essential Resources Contact Admissions Contact Athletics Make a Gift How-Tos Help Your Student Get Support Solve a Campus Life Problem Understand Finances, Records, and Family Access Quick Links Mail and Packages Academic Calendar Campus Life Student Health and Wellness Parent Giving and Engagement Essential Resources Parent and Family Portal Tuition and Billing Financial Aid Contact Student Life How-Tos Find the Right Person or Office Connect with Faculty Expertise Participate in Campus Life Quick Links University Calendar Campus Directory Schools and Departments University News Essential Resources MyTU Workday Faculty Profiles Staff Directory University Policies How-Tos Application Tips Guide for Student Athletes Guide for International Applicants Quick Links Majors and Minors Campus Life Undergraduate Research Academic Success Essential Resources Apply to Trinity Cost and Financial Aid Visit Trinity Request Information How-Tos Plan Your Campus Visit Get to and Around Campus Make the Most of Your Time in San Antonio Quick Links Events Calendar Campus Map Things to Do in San Antonio Essential Resources Visit Trinity Directions and Parking Virtual Tour Career-Engaged Learning Student Success arrow_drop_down Home Student Success Academic Success Accessibility and Accommodations Career-Engaged Learning Inclusion and Belonging Health and Wellbeing Career-Engaged Learning From internships and graduate school to meaningful careers and community engagement, Trinity students graduate prepared to lead lives of meaning and purpose. Pages in this section Career Planning arrow_right Internships arrow_right Volunteer and Service arrow_right Career and Internship Fairs arrow_right Recruit Trinity Students arrow_right Pages in this section Career Planning arrow_right Internships arrow_right Volunteer and Service arrow_right Career and Internship Fairs arrow_right Recruit Trinity Students arrow_right Your Purpose, In Action At Trinity, one of our core tenets is “Learning with Purpose.” From your first year through graduation, you’ll benefit from a highly personalized approach to career development, with individualized guidance and direct access to alumni, employers, and mentors. Strong Academics, Strong Support,  Strong Outcomes Your Trinity education begins with a first-year experience designed to help you explore your interests and consider different paths. Inside and outside the classroom, you’ll have opportunities to engage in community service, get involved, participate in exploratory and career-focused programs, build connections, and gain early hands-on experience. Whether you arrive with a clear direction or are still exploring, Trinity’s nationally recognized career advising team will help you connect those experiences to your goals. Along the way, you’ll gain the confidence and support to choose a major in the spring of your sophomore year and begin shaping what comes next. At Trinity, exploration, mentorship, hands-on learning, alumni access, and individualized support are intentionally woven into the student experience from day one. Facts & Stats 98% of graduates are employed or in grad school within 6 months 77% of students participate in research or internships 8,750 tracked volunteer hours annually 30,000+ alumni in the worldwide Tiger network, including 8,000 in greater San Antonio How We Help You Succeed You have ambitious goals. We’re here to help you reach them. Here’s how our team connects you to resources, people, and opportunities so you can thrive on campus and in your career. Career Planning and Exploration Career journeys are rarely linear. CELCS can help you explore interests, connect experiences to career possibilities, and build the skills, confidence, and network that prepare you for life after Trinity. Graduate School Guidance If you’re considering graduate or professional school, we can support you through the application process and connect you with resources to help you make informed decisions about your next steps. Internship Support Put learning into action through internships and other professional experiences. From finding opportunities to enrolling for credit, CELCS can help you navigate the process and gain valuable real-world experience. Individualized Job Search Assistance Build a strategic approach to your job search with support from CELCS. Explore opportunities, strengthen your resume, prepare for interviews, and learn how to confidently communicate the value of your experiences and skills. Alumni and Industry Networking Connect with Trinity alumni and industry partners through networking, recruiting, and educational events throughout the year. Trinity’s strong alumni and employer network helps you build meaningful connections and explore career opportunities early. Mentorship Build meaningful connections with Trinity alumni and mentors who can offer guidance, perspective, and support as you explore your interests and goals. Through conversations and shared experiences, , mentorship can help you grow your confidence, expand your network, and prepare for life after Trinity. Community Engagement and Service Make a meaningful impact while gaining valuable experience. Through community-engaged learning, volunteer opportunities, and partnerships with local organizations, you can connect your academic interests to real-world challenges, build professional skills, and contribute to the San Antonio community. arrow_right_alt Success Stories: Outcomes in Action More than 98% of recent graduates were employed or in graduate school within six months, continuing a strong track record of success with leading employers and graduate programs across the United States and abroad. Here are just a few of their stories. Valerie Arroyo ’25 shows just how far a Trinity education can take you. From building community through Greek Life to pursuing hands-on undergraduate research, she embraced every opportunity. From student-athlete at Trinity University to future Goldman Sachs analyst. Pierce Jackson ’25  turned a summer internship in business analytics and data science into a return offer after he graduates this spring. Urban Studies professor Christine Drennon, Ph.D. has paved the way for countless students to talk, think about, and engage with the cities around us in transformative ways, especially here at our home in San Antonio. Hear from her, and alumni like Victoria Lin Gonzalez-Gerlach '13, about the impact of the Urban Studies program. For Trinity stars like Starjjil Shelvin '19', the even smallest opening can lead to glory. From football player and standout engineering student to a promising career in IT and supply chain management, see “Star” reconnect with his Trinity professor, engineering professor Jack Leifer, and reminisce about how Trinity helps instill confidence in its students. Career Resources Wherever you are in your academic or career journey, Trinity is here to help you take the next step while connecting employers and organizations nationwide For Students open_in_new For Alumni arrow_right_alt For Employers arrow_right_alt For Faculty open_in_new For Staff open_in_new Career Connections I secured my first two internships at Dell through a combination of networking with alumni and utilizing resources like Trinity’s career fair. Ángel Santiago Gamarra ’25 Center for Experiential Learning and Career Success location_on Location Coates Student Center - Suite 215 call Phone 210-999-8321 drafts Emails Email 1 Trinity Place San Antonio, TX 78212 (210) 999-7011 Campus Directory News Athletics University Events University Calendars Library Maps and Directions Employment Courses of Study Bulletin Emergency Info Hire a Tiger The Trinity University Store MyTU Student Consumer Information Report an Incident University Policies Digital Accessibility © 2026 Trinity University. All rights reserved."
