      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers | Trinity University Skip to main content Utility Menu Apply Visit Give account_circle Info for manage_search Menu Search search Top Searches Main About Trinity Mission and Values Leadership and Governance Our Campus History and Traditions Strategy and Investment Trinity in San Antonio Academics Majors and Minors Pre-Professional Programs Graduate Programs Faculty Schools and Departments Academic Centers Study Abroad Research Faculty Research and Scholarship Undergraduate Research Centers and Facilities Access and Support Student Success Academic Success Accessibility and Accommodations Career-Engaged Learning Inclusion and Belonging Health and Wellbeing Campus Life Housing Dining Sports and Recreation Clubs and Organizations Safety Admissions and Aid Apply to Trinity Visit Campus Cost and Financial Aid Admitted Tigers Connect With Admissions Guides and Resources Utility Menu Apply Visit Give close Resources For Alumni Current Students Athletics Parents Faculty and Staff Prospective Students Visitors How-Tos Update Your Alumni Information Connect with the Trinity Network Volunteer and Give Back Quick Links Alumni Website Submit a Class Note Update My Information Find a Club Near You Request a Transcript Essential Resources Make a Gift Join the LinkedIn Group Share Your Story Buy Trinity Merchandise How-Tos Get Academic Support Find Your Community Solve a Campus Life Problem Quick Links Campus Events Academic Calendar Campus Dining Coates Library Essential Resources MyTU Workday Canvas Student Handbook Student Health Services How-Tos Guide for Student Athletes Quick Links Athletics Website Watch Tiger Network Athletics Instagram Bell Center Hours Essential Resources Contact Admissions Contact Athletics Make a Gift How-Tos Help Your Student Get Support Solve a Campus Life Problem Understand Finances, Records, and Family Access Quick Links Mail and Packages Academic Calendar Campus Life Student Health and Wellness Parent Giving and Engagement Essential Resources Parent and Family Portal Tuition and Billing Financial Aid Contact Student Life How-Tos Find the Right Person or Office Connect with Faculty Expertise Participate in Campus Life Quick Links University Calendar Campus Directory Schools and Departments University News Essential Resources MyTU Workday Faculty Profiles Staff Directory University Policies How-Tos Application Tips Guide for Student Athletes Guide for International Applicants Quick Links Majors and Minors Campus Life Undergraduate Research Academic Success Essential Resources Apply to Trinity Cost and Financial Aid Visit Trinity Request Information How-Tos Plan Your Campus Visit Get to and Around Campus Make the Most of Your Time in San Antonio Quick Links Events Calendar Campus Map Things to Do in San Antonio Essential Resources Visit Trinity Directions and Parking Virtual Tour Careers Office of Human Resources arrow_drop_down Home Office of Human Resources Open Positions Careers Employee Benefits Careers Pages in this section Employee Onboarding arrow_right Pages in this section Employee Onboarding arrow_right Find Your Career Trinity University aims to attract an efficient, dedicated staff whose talents will continue to grow the University as an exceptional place to study and work. Our mission provides every faculty and staff member the opportunity to make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, other staff, around San Antonio, and the world. Faculty Positions Staff Positions Student Employment at Trinity An essential part of Trinity's workforce is made up of the hundreds of students who participate in Student Employment and the Federal Work-study program. Essential Procedures & Requirements The Student Employment Policy outlines the procedures & requirements for students currently employed in a university office or department through part-time positions, both regular-wage or work-study and the supervising faculty and staff from Trinity University departments and offices who hire student workers. Applying for a Job: Step 1 Please review the list of vacant student positions available for Federal Work Study or Institutional Student Employment on Handshake , and select a job in which you are interested. Contact the department(s) of interest and schedule an interview. Departments looking to advertise a position, please complete and submit the On-Campus Student Employment Google Form (For Department Use Only).  The Center for Experiential Learning and Career Success will then post the open student position on Handshake. Step 2 Once your supervisor has officially hired you as a student worker in Workday , please come by Human Resources (Northrup Hall 210) to complete Form I-9. Per federal law, as an employer, Trinity University is required to verify your identity and employment authorization within your first 3 days of work. Students must provide original, unexpired documents that establish their identity and citizenship. Please see the I-9 List of Acceptable Documents . Step 3 Login to your Workday profile using your Trinity login credentials to complete the student onboarding process, which includes part 1 of your Form I-9 and your W-4/Federal Withholdings Elections. Please reference the Student Onboarding video for assistance. Student Employment Dates 2026 Spring: 1/14/26 – 5/16/26 Summer: 5/18/26 - 8/23/26 Fall: 8/24/26 - 12/23/26 Office of Human Resources location_on Location Northrup Hall call Phone 210-999-7507 fax Fax 210-999-7542 drafts Emails Email 1 Trinity Place San Antonio, TX 78212 (210) 999-7011 Campus Directory News Athletics University Events University Calendars Library Maps and Directions Employment Courses of Study Bulletin Emergency Info Hire a Tiger The Trinity University Store MyTU Student Consumer Information Report an Incident University Policies Digital Accessibility © 2026 Trinity University. All rights reserved."
