      "description": "Employee Onboarding | Trinity University Skip to main content Utility Menu Apply Visit Give account_circle Info for manage_search Menu Search search Top Searches Main About Trinity Mission and Values Leadership and Governance Our Campus History and Traditions Strategy and Investment Trinity in San Antonio Academics Majors and Minors Pre-Professional Programs Graduate Programs Faculty Schools and Departments Academic Centers Study Abroad Research Faculty Research and Scholarship Undergraduate Research Centers and Facilities Access and Support Student Success Academic Success Accessibility and Accommodations Career-Engaged Learning Inclusion and Belonging Health and Wellbeing Campus Life Housing Dining Sports and Recreation Clubs and Organizations Safety Admissions and Aid Apply to Trinity Visit Campus Cost and Financial Aid Admitted Tigers Connect With Admissions Guides and Resources Utility Menu Apply Visit Give close Resources For Alumni Current Students Athletics Parents Faculty and Staff Prospective Students Visitors How-Tos Update Your Alumni Information Connect with the Trinity Network Volunteer and Give Back Quick Links Alumni Website Submit a Class Note Update My Information Find a Club Near You Request a Transcript Essential Resources Make a Gift Join the LinkedIn Group Share Your Story Buy Trinity Merchandise How-Tos Get Academic Support Find Your Community Solve a Campus Life Problem Quick Links Campus Events Academic Calendar Campus Dining Coates Library Essential Resources MyTU Workday Canvas Student Handbook Student Health Services How-Tos Guide for Student Athletes Quick Links Athletics Website Watch Tiger Network Athletics Instagram Bell Center Hours Essential Resources Contact Admissions Contact Athletics Make a Gift How-Tos Help Your Student Get Support Solve a Campus Life Problem Understand Finances, Records, and Family Access Quick Links Mail and Packages Academic Calendar Campus Life Student Health and Wellness Parent Giving and Engagement Essential Resources Parent and Family Portal Tuition and Billing Financial Aid Contact Student Life How-Tos Find the Right Person or Office Connect with Faculty Expertise Participate in Campus Life Quick Links University Calendar Campus Directory Schools and Departments University News Essential Resources MyTU Workday Faculty Profiles Staff Directory University Policies How-Tos Application Tips Guide for Student Athletes Guide for International Applicants Quick Links Majors and Minors Campus Life Undergraduate Research Academic Success Essential Resources Apply to Trinity Cost and Financial Aid Visit Trinity Request Information How-Tos Plan Your Campus Visit Get to and Around Campus Make the Most of Your Time in San Antonio Quick Links Events Calendar Campus Map Things to Do in San Antonio Essential Resources Visit Trinity Directions and Parking Virtual Tour Employee Onboarding Careers arrow_drop_down Home Careers Employee Onboarding Employee Onboarding Pages in this section Employee Onboarding arrow_right Pages in this section Employee Onboarding arrow_right Congratulations, and welcome to Trinity University As a new employee, here is some information to help prepare you for your first week at Trinity. 1. Your Start Date August 2026 Monday, August 3 Monday, August 17 September 2026 Tuesday, September 7 Monday, September 14 October 2026 Monday, October 5 Monday, October 19 November 2026 Monday, November 2 Monday, November 16 December 2026 Monday, December 7 Monday, December 14 2. Relocation Resources If you need assistance with housing, hotels, schools, moving companies, hospitals, or any other city resources, contact HR at @email . Moving to Trinity from out of town? These resources should help make the move go smoothly. New Employee Moving Policy 3. On Your First Day Form I-9 and W-4 Come with original documents needed for the Form I-9 and W-4. Parking Permits Parking permits can be purchased in Student Financial Services, Northrup Hall 108A. Bring your valid drivers license, proof of insurance, and your license plate number. View our campus map for available parking lots. The Parking Services division can be reached at 210-999-7001. Tiger Card Obtain your Tiger Card ID (Storch Memorial Building 005). A Tiger Card is the University identification card that grants access to your building, the Bell Center, and the Library. New-Hire Mandatory Compliance Training All new hires are required to complete mandatory compliance training within the first 30 days of employment. Courses will be delivered via Workday Learning. New hires will receive a notification via email and their Workday inbox to complete their required courses. Login to Workday Learning Office of Human Resources location_on Location Northrup Hall call Phone 210-999-7507 fax Fax 210-999-7542 drafts Emails Email 1 Trinity Place San Antonio, TX 78212 (210) 999-7011 Campus Directory News Athletics University Events University Calendars Library Maps and Directions Employment Courses of Study Bulletin Emergency Info Hire a Tiger The Trinity University Store MyTU Student Consumer Information Report an Incident University Policies Digital Accessibility © 2026 Trinity University. All rights reserved."
